Abstract paintings use colors, lines, shapes, forms, and textures to create visual compositions that do not necessarily represent recognizable objects or scenes. Rather than focusing on realistic representation, these artworks emphasize visual expression, artistic interpretation, and conceptual ideas. They may incorporate geometric patterns, spontaneous brushstrokes, or unconventional arrangements of visual elements.
